      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s do this in a safer way. I don\u0027t think this is something that a Java app should be able to do.\n\nHere\u0027s my sketch.\n\n1. App uses `InputManager` APIs to get the `InputDevice`s for the external mouse and keyboard. Use `isExternal()` API.\n\n2. App asks `InputManager` to have exclusive access to the `InputDevice`s. This should require a privileged permission and should be granted only for external devices.\n\n3. If granted, InputManager returns FDs to the input devices.\n\n4. App passes those FDs to AVF when creating a VM.\n\n5. AVF passes that FDs to crosvm.\n\nI think this needs a small design doc to discuss with the team owning the input manager.",
